:true,"_score_margins":80.8,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.0,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":11.1,"_gate_share_shrink":0.03463065891502315,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":6.7,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.30793150251238954,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.01372,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":9.1,"_gate_insider_buying":0.071,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":7.1,"pf":[],"description_full":"Core Scientific, Inc. provides infrastructure for high-density colocation services and digital asset mining in the United States. It operates through three segments: Colocation, Digital Asset Self-Mining, and Digital Asset Hosted Mining. The company offers space, power, cooling, facilities operations, security, and other services to third-party customers to support workloads for machine learning and artificial intelligence; deployment, monitoring, troubleshooting, optimization, and maintenance of its customers' digital asset mining equipment; and electrical power, repair, and other infrastructure services for its customers to operate, maintain, and mine digital assets. It is also involved in the deployment and operation of its fleet of miners within its digital infrastructure as part of a pool of users that process transactions conducted on one or more blockchain networks to receive digital assets in the form of bitcoin. It also deploys and operates its fleet of miners within its digital infrastructure as part of a pool of users that process transactions conducted on one or more blockchain networks; and provides hosting services for digital asset mining customers, which include deployment, monitoring, trouble shooting, optimization, and maintenance of its customers' digital asset mining equipment. Core Scientific, Inc. was founded in 2017 and is headquartered in Dover, Delaware.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Adam  Sullivan | CEO, President & Director | Age 33 | Compensation: $2.9M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 325 people. Revenue per employee of $982K ranks in the top quartile among Technology peers, with revenue falling 21%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $302K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (9/10).","financial_summary":["Core Scientific, Inc. is a mid-cap technology business with a $4.7B market cap on $319M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -21% over the past three years, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Gross margins of 18% are the starting point for assessing pricing power.","The company is burning through $451M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, thin -16.2\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and stock-based comp at 31% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (-1.8) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (25.6% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Technology peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins 84% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Carries a 840% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":8.401675878053128},{"text":"Insiders are overwhelmingly selling (93% sell ratio) \u2014 the people who know the business want less of it","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.071},{"text":"Gross margin trails most Technology peers \u2014 competitors appear to have the pricing hand","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Core Scientific (CORZ) Stock Still Looks Above Fair Value On Its 26% Weekly Jump","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/software/nasdaq-corz/core-scientific/news/core-scientific-corz-stock-still-looks-above-fair-value-on-i","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794579514.84,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.945,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Surging Earnings Estimates Signal Upside for Core Scientific, Inc. (CORZ) Stock","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3028928/surging-earnings-estimates-signal-upside-for-core-scientific-inc-corz-stock?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cyseop_template_8-3028928","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794500402.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Wall Street Analysts See a 91.83% Upside in Core Scientific, Inc. (CORZ): Can the Stock Really Move This High?","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3028707/wall-